+# HAL Engine tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                 |
+| ------ | --------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress           |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema that is handed verbatim to both providers, and until now nothing checked what the model actually sent: a malformed tool call reached the executor as-is, where each executor improvised its own defence - a cast, a default, a confidently formatted answer for input that was never valid. The registry now validates every call's `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs, so a tool receives only input the schema accepts, and a malformed call comes back to the model as a tool result it can read and correct instead of ending the conversation. Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only: it injects no `additionalProperties: false`, coerces no types, applies no defaults, and offers no opt-out.
+
+## Registration
+
+- `register` compiles the resolved definition's `inputSchema` immediately, so a schema no validator accepts throws at registration - at startup, not mid-conversation - and the error names the tool ([validated by: refuses an uncompilable schema at registration, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration and the compiled validator reused across `execute` calls, so ten calls of one tool cost one compilation.
+
+## Validation, before the executor
+
+- `execute` validates the call's `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs: a call the schema rejects returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names what was wrong - a missing required property, for instance - and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property, naming it, without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A field whose value type differs from the declared one is rejected with a message naming the property path and the expected type ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, never the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- An `enum` constraint is enforced like any other: a value outside the declared set is rejected before the executor runs ([validated by: rejects a value outside an enum without leaking identifying input into result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+- A rejection names failing property paths and the constraint that failed, and carries no property value - not in the returned result, and not in any log line - because tool input is where identifying data enters the engine and the engine redacts nothing ([validated by: rejects a value outside an enum without leaking identifying input into result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged, including properties the schema does not declare, exactly once per call: no defaults injected, no types coerced ([validated by: passes accepted input through to the executor unchanged, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L50)).
+- An unregistered name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`, unchanged ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L160)).
+
+## Function-valued sources
+
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved per call, so validation uses the schema the source returns at that call rather than one captured earlier ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L136)).
+
+## The tool loop
+
+- A rejected call is returned to the provider as the tool's result rather than thrown, so `processMessage` resolves and the model can correct the call on a later round within the existing tool-round bound ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so the next round can correct it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L172)).
